Z||000008||FieroJoe||02-23-2001||09:41 PM||||At first I thought the dude was saying the "wind-grabber", was the over-the-top indy scoop.  But, the pictures say the car dosent have one.  So I'm stumped now too.  Maybe he's talking about the spoiler?<P>Good ole airbag and power seat trick!  I've always wondered if the people who have put these options *magically* into their Fiero have ever actually sold it on ebay...<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Archie||02-23-2001||10:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR><B>Was scanning through ebay and saw this, <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=563442634&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=563442634&r=0&t=0</A> <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This guy is hoping that some idiot will pop up on EBay and think that's a good deal.<P>While everybody is beating up on him, I'd like to point out that he is also guilty of one of my pet peeves.<P>I hate it when people post up pictures of Fieros for sale and can't even bother to pull the car outside in good light. Many times when they do pull the car outside, they take pictures in poor lighting or in shadows. They don't care what's in the background, I just saw one that had laundry hanging in the background. Not only does this guy take the pics. in the garage, he also has an open doorway in the background, great. I've seen people who post up pictures of some great new Fiero product or idea & the pictures are so out of focus, dark, or the subject matter incomplete or too dirty etc. that they would be better leaving the pictures out. <P>Give me a break. I certainly don't want to buy a car from someone who says the car is worth everything he wants for it yet he's to lazy to care about his presentation. When I see an auction or a Web Site that has poor pictures, I can't get out of there fast enough. Why in the heck  do so many people post pictures of cars up for sale that were taken outside at night with only the flash of the camera? .... Are they in such a hurry to put the thing up for sale that they can't wait for daylight?<P>Come on guys, tell your neighbors. If they want to sell a $2000 car for $8995, they should at least make it look as good as possible. Roll that sucker outside in the daylight! <P>I'm always in the market for a few more good Fieros, but I'll be darned if I'll even consider one that the seller can't manage to get a couple of good pictures of.<P>Ok, getting off of the out of focus Soapbox now.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||02-23-2001||10:35 PM||||Who cares about the mileage when they throw in a free Chilton manual and Car Cover??????||||reg||1
Z||000011||2xsess||02-23-2001||10:56 PM||||Another thing that annoys me about this one in particular, There's no interior shots!!!<P>I agree with you Archie, There really is no excuse for poor presentation <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
